图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"An in-process trigram index that makes code search in Pi&DSH 20-70x faster than ripgrep, with identical results and no sidecar process.","id":"gh:1333007619","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"snapgrep","slug":"Owen718/snapgrep","topics":["ai-coding-agent","code-search","coding-agent","deepseek-harness","developer-tools","dsh","dsh-plugin","grep","napi-rs","oh-my-pi","pi-agent","pi-coding-agent","ripgrep","rust","trigram-index"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"An in-process trigram index that makes code search in Pi&DSH 20-70x faster than ripgrep, with identi"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"cal results and no sidecar process."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"snapgrep"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"An in-process trigram index that makes code search in Pi"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Typically 40–70× faster than ripgrep on a warm index —"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"and every result is checked against ripgrep, byte for byte."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"No sidecar process. No daemon. A single 3.2 MB native addon loaded inside the agent process."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### Pi"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Pi's built-in `grep` is replaced automatically, in every project. To confirm, ask Pi to search for a"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" string you know exists — the tool detail shows `actualBackend: kernel`."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### oh-my-pi (omp)"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Same package, no changes: omp treats `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` as an aliased scope and its l"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"oader accepts `.pi` directories alongside `.omp`."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### DeepSeek Harness (dsh)"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Verify with `dsh --profile headless --dump-config | grep snapgrep`."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"It replaces both `grep` and `glob`: the registry rejects a duplicate tool name outright, so the buil"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"t-in search row is disabled and this plugin supplies both. `glob` runs the same ripgrep invocation t"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"s disabled and this plugin supplies both. `glob` runs the same ripgrep invocation the built-in used."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Only the addon your machine can run is downloaded — about 1.2 MB, two packages. Nothing is compiled "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"and no daemon is started."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Prebuilt for macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel), Linux (x64 and arm64, glibc), and Windows x64. Alpine/"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"musl is not built yet; on an unsupported platform the extension names the exact file it could not fi"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"nd rather than failing silently."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Other ways to install — no npm, single project, or one copy for every machine"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Without npm, a script fetches the matching archive from the latest release and installs into `~/.pi/"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ipt fetches the matching archive from the latest release and installs into `~/.pi/agent/extensions`:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Set `PI_EXTENSIONS_DIR` to install elsewhere. For a directory that works on any machine, `snapgrep-e"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"xtension-all-platforms.tar.gz` from the same release carries all five addons and picks the right one"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"latforms.tar.gz` from the same release carries all five addons and picks the right one at load time."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Into a single project rather than globally:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"`--approve` is only needed the first time, to trust a project-level extension. The artifact carries "},{"id":"p26s2","text":"a `.gitignore` scoped to its own directory, so installing it will not make your repository dirty."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Building from source: `npm run build:kernel && npm run package:extension`."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"中文安装说明见 安装说明.md。"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Why this exists"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Coding agents search constantly. Every `grep` call in a large repository means ripgrep reads every b"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"yte on disk again — hundreds of milliseconds, several times a minute, forever."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Index-backed search fixes that, but the usual answer is a sidecar daemon (Zoekt, and everything buil"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"t on it): another process to launch, supervise, keep in sync, and debug when it drifts. For a CLI ag"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"ent that starts and stops constantly, that is a lot of machinery."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"snapgrep puts the whole index in the agent's own process. Rust builds and queries a trigram index ov"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"er a git snapshot; Node calls it through N-API. Startup to first query is about half a second, and t"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"he index is smaller than the code it indexes."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Why a custom kernel"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Not because the trigram algorithm is novel. It isn't — Zoekt has done this well for years, and this "},{"id":"p34s2","text":"project measured itself against Zoekt on every accepted change."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"The reason is that buying the index means buying its process boundary, and the boundary costs more t"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"han the search. Here is where Zoekt's slowest query on the vite corpus actually spent its 18.32 ms:"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"| Stage | Time | Share |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Zoekt's own search | 1.24 ms | 7% |\n| HTTP transpor"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"t + JSON decode | 3.58 ms | 20% |\n| Verification (mostly `rg` process startup) | 8.34 ms | 45% |\n| L"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"ocal merge and classification | 5.14 ms | 28% |"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"**The search itself is 7% of the bill.** The other 93% is the cost of the index living somewhere els"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"e: serialise the query, cross a socket, decode JSON, then spawn ripgrep to re-read files the index a"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"lready had in memory. A single ripgrep spawn has a floor of about 6 ms on this machine — that alone "},{"id":"p37s4","text":"outweighs the entire search."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Owning the kernel is what makes that 93% disappear:"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"- **The index is mapped into the agent's own memory.** No socket, no JSON, no serialisation. A query"},{"id":"p39s2","text":" is a function call.\n- **Verification reads the mmap'd index, not the disk.** Candidates are confirm"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"ed in-process against bytes that are already resident, so there is no spawn and no second read.\n- **"},{"id":"p39s4","text":"Unsupported queries can fail closed instead of approximating.** This one is not a performance argume"},{"id":"p39s5","text":"nt, and it is the reason a general-purpose library was not enough. An earlier attempt used an off-th"},{"id":"p39s6","text":"e-shelf file finder for candidate selection; on the Linux kernel tree it returned 17,767 files where"},{"id":"p39s7","text":" ripgrep found 17,772. Five missing files, from nested `.gitignore` re-inclusion rules — and a final"},{"id":"p39s8","text":" ripgrep pass can only remove extra results, never recover ones the candidate stage already dropped."},{"id":"p39s9","text":" When the recall boundary is someone else's implementation detail, you cannot prove it, and you cann"},{"id":"p39s10","text":"ot fix it.\n- **The index format is tuned for this shape of data** — compressed content blocks, delta"},{"id":"p39s11","text":"-varint gram metadata — which is how the index lands at 0.38–0.91× the size of the source it indexes"},{"id":"p39s12","text":"varint gram metadata — which is how the index lands at 0.38–0.91× the size of the source it indexes."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"1. Split the pattern into trigrams and intersect their posting lists to get candidate files.\n2. Appl"},{"id":"p43s2","text":"y hidden / path / glob / case filters at the candidate level, before any file is read.\n3. Verify exa"},{"id":"p43s3","text":"ctly, in-process, over the mmap'd index — no subprocess, no re-read from disk.\n4. Materialize only t"},{"id":"p43s4","text":"he lines actually needed for the requested limit and context."},{"id":"p44s1","text":"The index is a single file per repository, built from a clean git snapshot, with content blocks comp"},{"id":"p44s2","text":"ressed and gram metadata delta-varint encoded."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
